Rule 1 (x and y must have the same type)
{x: tensor, y: tensor} |= dtype_(x) = dtype_(y)
>>
Rule 2 (x must be one of the allowed types: bfloat16, half, float32, float64, int32, int64, complex64, complex128. We represent it using a disjunction of allowed dtypes.)
{x: tensor} |= (dtype_(x) = 7) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 8) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 4) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 5) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 9) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 10) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 6)
>>
Rule 3 (x and y should have compatible shapes to avoid broadcasting errors - simplified version: same number of dimensions)
{x: tensor, y: tensor} |= ndim(x) = ndim(y)
>>
Rule 6 (If x is int32, then other types are not allowed)
{x: tensor} |= if dtype_(x) = 4 then true
>>
Rule 8 (name cannot be an empty string)
{name: str} |= name ≠ ""
>>
Rule 29 (At least one tensor should have positive number of dimensions)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= ndim(x) > 0 ∨ ndim(y) > 0
>>
Rule 56 (Check if tensors are scalar.)
{x: tensor, y: tensor} |= (ndim(x) = 0) ∨ (ndim(y) = 0)
>>
Rule 88 (Ndim should be non-negative)
{x: tensor} |= ndim(x) ≥ 0
